<%#
  Whether to tell the class.

  Ticked by default, because the reason to change a lesson in the first
  place is that people need to know. Unticking it is for the correction
  you make thirty seconds after the first one, when a second email would
  only confuse.

  When no mail server is configured the box is not shown at all, and it
  says so: an inviting tick box that silently does nothing is worse than
  no tick box.

  Expects: canEmail, verb.
%>
<% if (canEmail) { %>
  <label class="check">
    <input type="checkbox" name="notify" value="1" checked>
    <span>Email everyone on this batch about <%= verb %></span>
  </label>
<% } else { %>
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:.8rem;margin:.4rem 0 0">
    No mail server is set up, so nobody will be emailed.
    The change still shows in every student's portal.
  </p>
<% } %>
